.el .ds Aq '
.TH import 1  "import " 
.SH NAME
import \- Import snippet file(s) (`ForgeHub` or Forgenesis format)
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBimport\fR [\fB\-\-from\-forgenesis\fR] [\fB\-\-from\-gist\fR] [\fB\-\-registry\fR] [\fB\-\-name\fR] [\fB\-\-force\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fIFILE\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Import snippet file(s) (`ForgeHub` or Forgenesis format)
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-from\-forgenesis\fR
Import from the Forgenesis workflows directory instead ($`FORGENESIS_HOME/workflows` or ~/.forgenesis/workflows)
.TP
\fB\-\-from\-gist\fR \fI<FROM_GIST>\fR
Import a public GitHub Gist by URL: the server fetches it (ADR 0010) and imports its files as private snippets
.TP
\fB\-\-registry\fR \fI<REGISTRY>\fR
Registry base URL for \-\-from\-gist (default: `FORGEHUB_REGISTRY` or config)
.TP
\fB\-\-name\fR \fI<NAME>\fR
Save under a different name (single file only)
.TP
\fB\-\-force\fR
Overwrite existing snippets with the same name
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
[\fIFILE\fR]
A snippet file, or a directory of snippet files. Optional with \-\-from\-forgenesis
.SH EXTRA
Examples:
  fg import snippets.yaml
  fg import \-\-from\-forgenesis
